  "domain_interpretations": {
    "0": "Neuronal-rich cortical territory, distinguished by neuronal structural and synaptic transcripts (NEFL, SNAP25, TUBA1B); precise cortical layer uncertain.",
    "1": "Upper/supragranular-like cortical territory, suggested by CUX2, CALB2, HPCAL1 and CAMK2N1; layer assignment remains a hypothesis without histology.",
    "2": "Myelin-rich white-matter-like compartment, supported by coordinated MOBP, MAG, MBP, PLP1, CNP, and MOG enrichment.",
    "3": "Mixed transcriptomic patch with epithelial/immune-response-like signals (KRT19, HLA-B, IFI27) and neuronal signals; likely noncanonical tissue/technical signal, not confidently an anatomical layer.",
    "4": "Peripheral/edge-like territory with glial/vascular-associated candidates (CLU, SLC1A2, DES, ACTA2) and comparatively low UMI; susceptible to quality or dissection-edge effects.",
    "5": "Neuronal-rich territory with unusual secretory/epithelial-like transcripts (SCGB2A2, TFF1, MGP); a distinct expression domain, but anatomical identity uncertain and possible contamination.",
    "6": "Spatially less cohesive mixed/intermediate territory with neuronal (DIRAS2, SLC17A7, SEMA3E) and unusual epithelial-associated (KRT17, SCGB1D2) signals; not confidently an anatomical layer or gray-white interface."
  },
